Vendored agent core
===================

Contains code from https://github.com/earendil-works/pi (MIT), commit c1d4b0a.

The vendored subset is pi's CORE agent functions only — the agent loop with
tool calling, plus its pi-schema JSON Schema validator and the pi-ai
message/transcript/event-stream utilities the loop needs:

  pi-agent/   <- packages/agent/src/{types,stream-fn,agent-loop}.ts
  pi-ai/      <- packages/ai/src/{types.ts, providers/{compat-schema,model-schema,schema-builders}.ts,
                 utils/{diagnostics,event-stream,identity,text,transcript,validation,version}.ts}
  pi-schema/  <- packages/schema/src/** (complete)

pi-ai/LICENSE and pi-schema/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES/typebox-LICENSE: the schema
format checks are adapted from TypeBox 1.3.27 (MIT).

Deviations from upstream (kept minimal, for the Cloudflare Workers runtime):
- import specifiers rewritten from package names ("@earendil-works/pi-ai",
  "@earendil-works/pi-schema") to relative paths inside this vendor tree.
- pi-ai/types.ts: dropped the @earendil-works/pi-telemetry import/field and the
  ApiOptionsMap/ApiStreamOptions types (they drag in pi-ai's api/* provider
  adapters, which are not vendored — the Worker uses its own BYOK adapters).
- pi-ai/utils/identity.ts: dropped the models.ts catalog types and the
  process-based User-Agent formatting (no `process` global on Workers).
- everything else is byte-identical to upstream, tabs and `.ts`-suffixed
  imports included, to keep future upstream sync diffs small.

